    "body": "Design decision for the owner (M5), with the recommended option taken. The first slice doesn't depend on it.\n\nThere is no user machine folder or search path today: the only user `.mch` the app reads is the one a document mounts through Setup > Load other. So the first slice lists the built-in machines plus that file, and its `scan_dir` hook is ready for a folder.\n\n**Recommended (taken for the follow-ups):** resolve a user machines folder the way theme files are resolved (`crates/ui/src/theme_dir.rs`):\n1. a `CAMCRAFT_MACHINES` environment override;\n2. otherwise a writable per-user `<platform data dir>/camcraft/machines`.\n\nThe pane scans it, and the editor's Save As writes there. Shipped machines stay read-only.\n\n**Considered and dropped:** a folder setting stored in the project file. It ties a machine library to one document, so it travels badly between projects.\n\nRecorded in `docs/decisions/287-machines-pane.md`.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
